kosha alkane

  -- saturated hydrocarbons: CnH2n+2. only single C-C and C-H bonds.
  -- saturated = no double or triple bonds. carbon is fully bonded.
  -- naming: methane (C1), ethane (C2), propane (C3), butane (C4),
  --         pentane (C5), hexane (C6), heptane (C7), octane (C8).
  -- tetrahedral geometry at each carbon (sp3 hybridisation).
  -- non-polar: no partial charges. insoluble in water. soluble in organic solvents.
  -- low reactivity: no functional group. only reaction: combustion and halogenation.
  -- combustion: CnH2n+2 + O2 → CO2 + H2O + heat (fossil fuels are alkanes).
  -- methane: natural gas, CH4, simplest alkane. greenhouse gas.
  -- octane: C8H18, petrol/gasoline. octane rating measures resistance to knocking.
  -- cycloalkanes: ring form CnH2n — cyclohexane, cyclopentane.

